  "deviations": [
    {
      "id": "owned-eval-program-lowering-not-implemented-here",
      "summary": "Plan §3.2.2 + W1B note 1 specify that OwnedTypeResolutionContext::declaration_fingerprints should be populated at lowering time, and that the EvalEnvCacheDb should store Arc<OwnedEvalProgram> as the canonical D46 representation. The lowering pipeline that produces OwnedEvalProgram from a parse does not exist at HEAD (host_executor.rs::execute_source produces ParseSnapshot + AnalysisSnapshot; no owned-artifact lowering pass). Tier 1C-α therefore: (a) preserves the legacy Arc<EvalEnv> cache inside EvalEnvCacheDb.legacy_env_entries so existing callers keep working with deterministic env reuse; (b) keeps the 1A Arc<OwnedEvalProgram> storage in place (used by tests today, by host_executor lowering when implemented); (c) does NOT populate declaration_fingerprints. The discriminating tests verify the storage shape contract (owned-program payload type, owned-context payload type) without requiring lowering to be wired through host_executor.",
      "files": [
        "crates/verter_session/src/host_executor.rs (no owned-artifact lowering pass)",
        "crates/verter_session/src/owned_artifacts/type_resolution_context.rs (declaration_fingerprints field present but populated by callers; not populated at lowering time)",
        "crates/verter_session/src/host_manage/eval_env.rs (cache_eval_env_arc + clone_cached_eval_env_arc delegate to legacy_env_entries)"
      ],
      "scope_implication": "MetaSession::assemble_surface_from_analysis still stamps query_path: None for NamedTypeHandles (W1B 1B placeholder); flipping this requires the lowering pipeline that 1C-α does not implement. The BFS bridge's lazy frontier walk falls back to depth=0 on the first call. SemanticGraphStore::execute_cooperative_batch remains a warm-only probe (returns EvictedNode for cold keys). Tier 1C-α scope strictly covers the field rehoming + discriminating tests + arch-guard tightening; the lowering work + cold-admission extension belongs to a follow-up step."
    },
    {
      "id": "compile-cache-super-shape-preserved-not-split",
      "summary": "Plan §3.4.1 explicitly states 'CompileCacheEntry stays super-shape' (option (b)) — the CompileCacheDb wraps DashMap<String, CompileCacheEntry> verbatim. The split into ProfileState / DerivedRawState / DependencyState per the §3.4.2 invalidation matrix is dispatched as Step 1C-β.",
      "files": ["crates/verter_session/src/project_type_store.rs (CompileCacheDb.entries: DashMap<String, CompileCacheEntry>)"]
    },
    {
      "id": "host-accessor-method-form-not-typed-wrapper-form",
      "summary": "VerterHost.compile_cache() returns &DashMap<String, CompileCacheEntry> (the inner storage), not &CompileCacheDb (the wrapper). Rationale: 60+ existing call sites use `host.compile_cache.entry(...) / .get(...) / .iter() / .remove(...)` — DashMap method shapes. Returning the inner DashMap preserves all those shapes via field-to-method conversion (`.compile_cache.foo` → `.compile_cache().foo`). Returning &CompileCacheDb would have required adding 10+ wrapper methods (entry_or_default, get, get_mut, iter, iter_mut, remove, clear, len, is_empty, ...) just to mirror DashMap. The wrapper form is the right destination once the 1C-β CompileCacheEntry split lands and the call sites need typed accessors per ProfileState / DerivedRawState / DependencyState; doing it in 1C-α would have been speculative API design.",
      "files": ["crates/verter_session/src/host_construction.rs (compile_cache() returns &DashMap)"]
    }
  ],
